# origin/main behaviour (baseline per maintainer decision 6), with the P0.8 hazard gates below
# Generated by TestOperationGoldens (pkg/characterization); regenerate with -update. Do not edit.
# Operation: MenuManager.HardenSystem -> SecurityManager.HardenSystem (user, SSH, UFW, DNS)
# Reached by: hardn -r (cmd/hardn/main.go:230-260); menu Run All option 1 makes the same call with AllowedPorts=cfg.UfwAllowedPorts (pkg/menu/run_all_menu.go:226-268), in live mode only after a typed 'yes' (run_all_menu.go:155)
# FIXED (P0.8, gated by dryRunFlagApplies): V1 — hardn -n refuses every operation flag with exit status 2 before the root check, so nothing runs; the cfg.DryRun=true section is what the layers below the menus still do with DryRun set (A1), which no CLI flag reaches now
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V6 — password auth disabled and AuthenticationMethods publickey set in the same step that adds keys; nothing proves a key works
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V7 — no sshd -t before the restart and no sshd -T after; restart instead of reload
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V8 — the SSH port changes (sshd restart) before any firewall rule allows the new port
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V9 — ufw default deny, disable and reset run before the allow rule; only cfg.SshPort is allowed, not the effective sshd port
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V11 — PermitRootLogin no is forced regardless of config
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V14 — Alpine: sudo is never installed; the user is only added to wheel
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V15 — Alpine: the whole /etc/ssh/sshd_config is replaced (no Subsystem sftp, no Include)
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V16 — sudoers file written without visudo -c and non-atomically; the overwrite drops any env_keep line
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V17 — the user is created without a password
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V18 — writes are non-atomic and nothing is backed up first
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V19 — DNS: /etc/resolv.conf overwritten in place (a write through a symlink lands in its target); domain and search lan forced
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V21 — Alpine: root writes /home/<user>/.ssh/authorized_keys (home path assumed; write follows symlinks)
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V24 — a single AuthorizedKeysFile drops v0.3.2's ~/.ssh_<user>/authorized_keys, so keys on upgraded hosts stop working
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V27 — ListenAddress 0.0.0.0 makes sshd IPv4-only
# FIXED (P0.8, gated by runAllWithoutConfirmation): A4 — Run All option 1 asks for a typed 'yes' before a live run, and any other answer cancels with nothing applied; hardn -r does not ask. Not observed by this harness: pkg/menu's TestRunAllConfirmation and run_all/option1-live-cancel.golden record it
# NOTE: cfg.DryRun is set on the config passed to ServiceFactory.SetConfig, as cmd/hardn/main.go:158 does for -n (which now reaches only the menus). No layer below pkg/menu reads it.
# NOTE: HardeningConfig is built as cmd/hardn/main.go:234-250 builds it; SshKeyPaths is left empty, so the adapter writes its default AuthorizedKeysFile.
# NOTE: Proxmox check (pkg/adapter/secondary/proxmox.go), once per ServiceFactory, before the first SSH root-login or UFW decision: osdetect's IsProxmox (set on the proxmox cell, so it probes nothing), else /etc/pve, else dpkg-query's pve-manager status, which must read 'install ok installed' (the mock's empty output reads as not installed; Alpine is not asked).

